<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    RUT_TheForge                                   UtinniPatches - authored 2026-09-09
    BIOME_OWNERSHIP_WAVE_1. Full sheet: design/Jawa/worldbuilding/biomes/
    the_forge.md (FROZEN). "Defines three defs as one place" (sheet SS0, owner:
    "combining them is very welcome") — this ONE owned def replaces all three thin
    donors: `AB_PyroclasticConflagration` (Alpha Biomes, ash skirts), `LavaField`
    (Odyssey, the flows) and `Volcano` (Advanced Biomes, the cones). The sheet's own
    roster (rosters/the_forge.json) ALREADY lands one unified fauna/flora list for
    all three defNames ("ONE roster for all three defs... the sheet distinguishes
    zones by elevation, not fauna") — confirmed by extraction (identical entries
    across all three donor cast-patch blocks) — so merging the def is not inventing
    a new decision, it is following the roster's own already-ruled shape. Which of
    the three donor defNames' worker/texture/terrain to inherit is this def's one
    real choice: took AB_PyroclasticConflagration's (Alpha Biomes) as the base, since
    its terrain family (black pebbles/hardened grass) is the closest visual match to
    "obsidian gloss, ash grey, seam-red" (sheet SS9) of the three donors.

    MEASURED (sheet SS0): 44 tiles, one compact massif in the Dune Sea interior.
    Zonation by elevation: Volcano median 1,875 m (cones), LavaField median 2,010 m
    (flows), Pyroclastic median 1,382 m (skirts) — all inside this ONE def now.
    Dayside sun +51..+64 deg, temps 42-56 C.

    allowRivers FALSE: hard ban 6 ("No ordinary rain — the closed boiling cycle
    only") plus SS3's "the massif is its own weather engine... the only rain in the
    Dune Sea" argues no ordinary river network belongs here; the donor
    AB_PyroclasticConflagration itself already carries allowRivers false.

    Weather: rebuilt around SS3's closed boiling-rain cycle and ban 6 — ordinary
    Rain/RainyThunderstorm/Snow all zeroed. AB_VolcanicAsh/AB_VolcanicAshRain (Alpha
    Biomes WeatherDefs, MayRequire-gated) kept from the donor as the nearest existing
    stand-in for "sudden violent boiling rain that flashes back to steam... within
    seconds" (SS3) — a bespoke Scald-type WeatherDef for the Forge's own boiling
    rain is still un-owed (`FORGE_MECHANICS_1`, SS Owed) and NOT invented here.
    RSW_SW_RedFog kept MayRequire-gated per the donor's own live weather table
    (matches the def dump's currently-active entry on this donor).

    diseases trimmed to the vanilla-adjacent set (dropped BMT_Disease_Mutapox);
    diseaseMtbDays kept at the Pyroclastic donor's own 65 (not disputed by the
    sheet).

    WYYYSCHOKK_FERALISK_MERGE_1 (2026-09-10): AA_Cinderlisk and BMT_Maguana
    removed from wildAnimals: owner sitting ruling retired Alpha Animals'
    whole '-lisk' clade (Cherry Picker cut); both defNames stop resolving
    once that cut takes effect, and an unresolved cross-ref in wildAnimals
    is a known crash (BIOME_CAST_REFS_BREAK_MAPGEN_1).
    2026-09-18: the maguana is BACK as RSW_Maguana - ported into our own
    bestiary (CAVERNS_PARITY_BUILD_1 r5, owner: "the Forge keeps its
    creature"), so the resolution hazard above no longer applies to it;
    the donor's BMT_Maguana stays Cherry-Picked and must not be re-wired.

    plantDensity/animalDensity kept close to the Pyroclastic donor's own values
    (0.4/1.2): ban 3 ("No furred, chilled, or lush-register fauna — heat-adapted and
    few") argues sparse, matching the donor read rather than the higher LavaField/
    Volcano donor figures.

    wildAnimals/wildPlants: transplanted from BiomeCast_Ashkarr.xml /
    BiomeFlora_Ashkarr.xml against rosters/the_forge.json, using ONLY the
    AB_PyroclasticConflagration cast-patch block (all three donor blocks carry
    IDENTICAL entries per the roster's own "one roster" ruling — concatenating all
    three would have produced duplicate XML child elements).

    NOT this pass's scope: `FORGE_MECHANICS_1` (boiling-rain weather, beldon herd +
    tibanna harvest, vapor-column flight layer, tower dungeon shell, the Contagion
    die-off ring); `TIBANNA_EMBARGO_PLOT_1`; nothing lives in the lava (ban 1 — the
    moving machines in the melt are never a roster entry, matched: none of this
    def's wildAnimals is lava-native); any world repaint.

  -->

  <BiomeDef>
    <defName>RUT_TheForge</defName>
    <label>the Forge</label>
    <description>One mountain, three zones, and the only vertical skyline in the Dune Sea: tall, dark foundry towers rising defiantly against the sun, streaming vent-steam like banners, visible for a hundred kilometres. Below them the red seams and the flows; around them the ash skirts; above them, improbably, herds -- vast placid gas-grazers drifting in the vapor columns. The mountain rains on itself in scalding bursts, and mosses drink in the seconds between fall and flash.</description>
    <workerClass>AlphaBiomes.BiomeWorker_PyroclasticConflagration</workerClass>
    <foragedFood>AB_RawBrownBarrelCactus</foragedFood>
    <allowRoads>true</allowRoads>
    <allowRivers>false</allowRivers>
    <allowFarmingCamps>true</allowFarmingCamps>
    <animalDensity>1.2</animalDensity>
    <plantDensity>0.4</plantDensity>
    <forageability>0.5</forageability>
    <movementDifficulty>1.5</movementDifficulty>
    <texture>Biomes/AB_PyroclasticConflagration</texture>
    <diseaseMtbDays>65</diseaseMtbDays>
    <diseases>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_Flu</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>100</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_Plague</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>100</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_GutWorms</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>60</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_MuscleParasites</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>60</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_FibrousMechanites</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>30</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_SensoryMechanites</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>30</commonality>
      </li>
    </diseases>
    <terrainsByFertility>
      <li>
        <terrain>AB_BlackPebbles</terrain>
        <min>-999</min>
        <max>0.7</max>
      </li>
      <li>
        <terrain>AB_HardenedGrass</terrain>
        <min>0.7</min>
        <max>0.9</max>
      </li>
      <li>
        <terrain>AB_HardenedGrassFertile</terrain>
        <min>0.9</min>
        <max>999</max>
      </li>
    </terrainsByFertility>
    <baseWeatherCommonalities>
      <Clear>40</Clear>
      <AB_VolcanicAsh MayRequire="sarg.alphabiomes">20</AB_VolcanicAsh>
      <AB_VolcanicAshRain MayRequire="sarg.alphabiomes">6</AB_VolcanicAshRain>
      <RSW_SW_RedFog MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">8</RSW_SW_RedFog>
      <Rain>0</Rain>
      <RainyThunderstorm>0</RainyThunderstorm>
      <SnowGentle>0</SnowGentle>
      <SnowHard>0</SnowHard>
    </baseWeatherCommonalities>
    <wildAnimals>
      <AA_Aerofleet MayRequire="sarg.alphaanimals">0.4</AA_Aerofleet>  <!-- aerofleet - sky, adjust-keep -->
      <LavaSnail MayRequire="sarg.alphabiomes">0.35</LavaSnail>  <!-- lava snail - ground-slow, import -->
      <LavaFlea MayRequire="mlie.starwarsanimalcollection">0.25</LavaFlea>  <!-- lava flea - ground-herd, import -->
      <AA_Metallovore MayRequire="sarg.alphaanimals">0.15</AA_Metallovore>  <!-- metallovore - ground-slow, keep -->
      <Beldon MayRequire="mlie.starwarsanimalcollection">0.08</Beldon>  <!-- beldon - sky-herd, keep -->
      <RSW_Maguana MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.5</RSW_Maguana>  <!-- maguana - ground-slow, ported out of Caverns (CAVERNS_PARITY_BUILD_1 r5, owner: the Forge keeps its creature); donor commonality -->
      <!-- ECOSYSTEM_PYRAMID_LAW_1 (owner, 2026-09-20: "50% small"): this roster read
           43.4% small. This addition is already an OWNER-RULED member of this exact
           biome's fauna list (design/Jawa/worldbuilding/biomes/rosters/the_forge.json
           "fauna", 0.5) that was never wired — not invented. AA_CrescendoAnole
           (bodySize 0.3) is small; the roster's other two unwired entries
           (AA_ColossalAerofleet bodySize 2, Tibidee bodySize 12) are both LARGE and are
           left out on purpose. -->
      <AA_CrescendoAnole MayRequire="sarg.alphaanimals">0.5</AA_CrescendoAnole>  <!-- crescendo anole - small, ruled -->
      <!-- COMMISSION_LEDGER_CLEANUP_1: the_forge sheet's own owed roster line ("fleet
           fliers, flash-flora + fireweed") plus §4's named sky fauna ("small darting
           things that race in, eat fireweed, and retreat before they perish").
           RUT_FleetFlier.xml, this same pass, same mod (UtinniPatches) as this
           BiomeDef, so no MayRequire (matches the bare RUT_FireLavender/RUT_Sagecrust/
           RUT_HeatsinkFungus entries already in this file's own wildPlants list). -->
      <RUT_FleetFlier>0.45</RUT_FleetFlier>  <!-- fleet flier - small sky, new -->
    </wildAnimals>
    <coastalWildAnimals />
    <wildPlants>
      <Plant_Fireweed>0.9</Plant_Fireweed>  <!-- fireweed -->
      <Plant_MagmaCactus>0.7</Plant_MagmaCactus>  <!-- magma cactus -->
      <RUT_FireLavender>0.6</RUT_FireLavender>  <!-- fire lavender -->
      <RUT_Sagecrust>0.4</RUT_Sagecrust>  <!-- sagecrust -->
      <IronScruff_PrimordialGrass>0.35</IronScruff_PrimordialGrass>  <!-- primordial grass -->
      <!-- SHEET_ORPHAN_CONSUMPTION_1, owner review 2026-09-11: AG_Gamma, AG_Septimum and
           AB_GiantGamma all moved OUT of here to forsaken_crags ("to crags" / "elsewhere,
           not heat resistant") — this biome's 42-56 C floor is above their optimal band
           (opt max 42 C, MEASURED plant_pool.csv) and AB_GiantGamma was already resident
           at the crags. The ruling landed in rosters/the_forge.json and reached the game
           only through BiomeFlora_Ashkarr.xml's now-retired replace operation;
           transplanted here by BIOMEFLORA_PATCH_WIPES_WILDPLANTS_1. -->
      <AB_TinkleGrass>0.3</AB_TinkleGrass>  <!-- tinkle grass -->
      <IronScruff_PrimordialTallGrass>0.3</IronScruff_PrimordialTallGrass>  <!-- primordial tall grass -->
      <IronScruff_Bindweed>0.25</IronScruff_Bindweed>  <!-- bindweed -->
      <AB_FirevineTree>0.2</AB_FirevineTree>  <!-- firevine tree - tree -->
      <RUT_HeatsinkFungus>0.2</RUT_HeatsinkFungus>  <!-- heatsink fungus - tree -->
    </wildPlants>
    <wildPlantRegrowDays>27</wildPlantRegrowDays>
  </BiomeDef>

</Defs>
